{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates C++ code to Python 3 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following GNU C++ code to Python 3 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original GNU C++ code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n#include <iostream>\nusing namespace std;\n\ntypedef long long ll;\n\nint digitCount(ll x) {\n    int cnt = 0;\n    while (x > 0) {\n        x /= 10;\n        ++cnt;\n    }\n    return cnt;\n}\n\nll largestRepunit(ll x) {\n    int d = digitCount(x);\n    ll res = 0;\n    for (int i = 0; i < d; ++i) {\n        res = res * 10 + 1;\n    }\n    if (res <= x) return res;\n    return res / 10;\n}\n\nll solve(ll x) {\n    if (x <= 6) return x;\n    if (x <= 11) return 13 - x;\n    \n    ll rep = largestRepunit(x);\n    ll nextRep = rep * 10 + 1;\n    \n    if (x % rep == 0) {\n        if (x <= nextRep / 2 + rep) {\n            return digitCount(rep) * x / rep;\n        }\n        return digitCount(nextRep) + solve(nextRep - x);\n    } else {\n        ll base = (x / rep) * rep;\n        ll option1 = solve(base) + solve(x - base);\n        ll option2 = digitCount(nextRep) + solve(nextRep - x);\n        if (x > nextRep / 2) {\n            return min(option1, option2);\n        }\n        return option1;\n    }\n}\n\nint main() {\n    ll n;\n    cin >> n;\n    cout << solve(n) << endl;\n    return 0;\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\ndef digitCount(x):\n    cnt = 0\n    while x > 0:\n        x //= 10\n        cnt += 1\n    return cnt\n\ndef largestRepunit(x):\n    d = digitCount(x)\n    res = 0\n    for i in range(d):\n        res = res * 10 + 1\n    if res <= x:\n        return res\n    return res // 10\n\ndef solve(x):\n    if x <= 6:\n        return x\n    if x <= 11:\n        return 13 - x\n    \n    rep = largestRepunit(x)\n    nextRep = rep * 10 + 1\n    \n    if x % rep == 0:\n        if x <= nextRep // 2 + rep:\n            return digitCount(rep) * x // rep\n        return digitCount(nextRep) + solve(nextRep - x)\n    else:\n        base = (x // rep) * rep\n        option1 = solve(base) + solve(x - base)\n        option2 = digitCount(nextRep) + solve(nextRep - x)\n        if x > nextRep // 2:\n            return min(option1, option2)\n        return option1\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    n = int(input())\n    print(solve(n))\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n1.0\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-5.793403761344962e-05, -7.152555099310121e-07, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -0.0005144941387698054, -4.768370445162873e-07, -0.3133295476436615, -3.576278118089249e-07, -0.0007728926721028984, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -1.3708974620385561e-05, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0, -7.152555099310121e-07, 0.0, -8.129743218887597e-05, -4.768370445162873e-07, -1.1920928244535389e-07, 0.0, 0.0, -5.960462772236497e-07, -2.3841855067985307e-07, 0.0, -9.536697689327411e-06, 0.0, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -1.7881377516459906e-06, -2.3841574147809297e-05, -1.1920928244535389e-07, 0.0, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -3.4570634852570947e-06, -1.7881377516459906e-06, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -3.361645576660521e-05, -1.7881377516459906e-06, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -2.0265558760002023e-06, -8.22540732769994e-06, -2.145764938